<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00001778> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00001778> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-01"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "TIP39-PTH2R signaling, keratinocyte differentiation (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human TIP39 (PTH2) activates PTH2R in keratinocytes, raising cytosolic Ca2+ via PLC signaling and promoting keratinocyte differentiation."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Gs arm added: a second PTH2R activity unit directly activates Gs (GNAS G protein activity) in adenylate cyclase-activating GPCR signaling, from the cryo-EM PTH2R-TIP39-Gs structure and TIP39-induced cAMP in HEK293T (PMID:34353904); not shown in keratinocytes, and the adenylyl cyclase isoform is unknown, so the arm stops at Gs."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Human TIP39 (PTH2) acting from the extracellular region on PTH2R in epidermal keratinocytes, increasing cytosolic Ca2+ from ER stores via a PLC/IP3R-dependent route and promoting keratinocyte differentiation (PMID:27000502, PMID:28094886; ligand-receptor activation PMID:34353904). Gq, PLC and IP3R isoforms are not identified in the source papers (pharmacological inhibitors only) and are therefore not modelled. GO:0005576 used because GO:0005615 extracellular space is obsolete (replaced_by GO:0005576)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "IVL arm added: PTH2R (PLC pathway unit) causally upstream of PKCdelta (IC: TIP39 raises involucrin via PTH2R, PMID:27000502; calcium-induced involucrin requires PKCdelta, PMID:11864971; with GO:0007200) -> HRAS -> MAP3K1 (MEKK1) -> MAP2K3 (MEK3) -> MAPK13 (p38delta) -> CEBPA -> IVL, from dominant-negative epistasis in human keratinocytes (PMID:12080077, abstract only). Intra-cascade edges are 'causally upstream of, positive effect' because direct mechanisms were not shown; p38delta is reported to be activated by MKK6 in vitro (PMID:9218798). HRAS chosen for generic dominant-negative Ras. The PTH2R->PKCdelta join is a curator inference, not tested for TIP39. KRT14 arm not modelled (no evidence linking Ca2+/PKC to loss of deltaNp63)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

